  "instructions": [
    "Break up any clumps in the cold rice with your hands. Beat the eggs in a small bowl with a pinch of the salt.",
    "Heat 1 tbsp oil in a 12 inch nonstick skillet over medium-high heat. Pour in the eggs and stir until just set, about 1 minute. Move them to a plate.",
    "Add 1 tbsp oil to the skillet. Add the chicken, the remaining salt, and the white pepper. Cook, stirring now and then, for 5 to 6 minutes, until browned and no pink remains.",
    "Move the chicken to the plate with the eggs. Add the remaining 1 tbsp oil, the peas, and the carrots to the skillet. Cook for 2 minutes, until hot.",
    "Add the garlic and cook for 30 seconds, until fragrant.",
    "Add the rice and soy sauce. Stir and press the rice into the pan for 3 to 4 minutes, until hot and slightly toasted.",
    "Return the chicken and eggs to the skillet, breaking the eggs into small pieces. Check that the chicken reads 165 F, then stir in the green onions and serve."
  ],
